  "sourceRef": "SARS PAYE-GEN-01-G21 (2027) Rev 1 p. 31-32 (leave pay on termination taxed as a bonus, 3605); Magistrates' Courts Act 32 of 1944 s61 ('emoluments'), s65J(1)(b)(i), s65J(1A)(a); Maintenance Act 99 of 1998 s1 ('emoluments'), s28(1), s29(3) (Juta consolidations on justice.gov.za, read 2026-11-26); Hein rulings 6 and 15 (wave 7)",
  "notes": "As termination-garnishee-leave-pay, plus R50 000 severance (3901) on the line. Severance is never attached (ruling 6): the 25% stays on the R10 000 leave pay, 2500.00 of the R5 000 instalment. No directive is modelled, so the line takes no PAYE on the 3901 lump sum (the engine's rule without a directive; production pays severance only at a directive's figures). PAYE 2192.00 (leave pay alone); net 60 000 - 2 192 - 2 500 = 55 308.00. With 3901 in the base the cap would be 15 000 and the full R5 000 taken (net 52 808.00).",
